    <description>ALF-RS-04 FR5/FR6: fires when the Used Car Team records InitialValue on an AppraisalItem for the first time. Sets AF_ApprovalStatus__c=Pending, snapshots AF_PreviousInitialValue__c, notifies the Used Car Team queue, and submits the item into AF_AP_AppraisalItem_Manager - all in ONE flow interview reacting directly to the user&apos;s save.

MERGED 2026-09-12 (real bug found live): this used to be split into two flows - this one only set AF_ApprovalStatus__c=Pending, and a separate AF_FL_AppraisalItem_EvaluationSubmit (triggered off that field reaching Pending) did the notify+submit. That two-flow chain reliably faulted: submitting for approval from a flow that itself was triggered by ANOTHER flow&apos;s write in the same transaction hit a generic, unrecoverable &quot;unhandled fault&quot; from the submit action - proven by isolating every other variable (queue setup, both Appraisal validation rules, field values, transaction model) and confirming identical field writes succeed when done directly (bypassing this flow via AF_SkipReEvaluation__c) but fail every time when this flow&apos;s own Update_Item triggers the second flow&apos;s submit. The submit action only supports flowTransactionModel=CurrentTransaction (confirmed - NewTransaction is rejected at deploy), so the fix is structural: do the notify+submit here, directly, so submit is one flow deep from the user&apos;s save instead of two. AF_FL_AppraisalItem_EvaluationSubmit is now deactivated/unused - nothing else sets AF_ApprovalStatus__c to Pending on this object.

The original 2026-09-08 concern this split was built to solve (two AppraisalItems getting InitialValue set in the same transaction each independently reaching Submit_For_Approval) is still safe here: each item&apos;s own interview only ever submits ITSELF (objectId=$Record.Id), so two sibling items in one transaction each run their own independent Update_Item + Get_Existing_Process + Submit_For_Approval sequence with no shared key to race on - the original race was specific to the OLD per-Appraisal design (both interviews writing the SAME Appraisal row), which no longer applies now that approval is per-item.

Get_Existing_Process is scoped to Status=Pending only (not Approved/Rejected) so a genuine resubmission after a prior decision still gets submitted, while an actual in-flight duplicate is skipped.</description>
